{"step_index":165,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:33:45Z","content":"### Clarification & Update on Q32 (Chapter 4: Determinants)\n\nIn the CBSE / NCERT Class XII curriculum:\n- **Chapter 3 is Matrices:** Operations, Transpose, Symmetric/Skew-Symmetric matrices. (Allocated 3 MCQs + 1 SA (3m) + 1 Case Study (4m) = **10 Marks** in the blueprint).\n- **Chapter 4 is Determinants:** Minors, Cofactors, Adjoint, Inverse of a Matrix ($A^{-1} = \\frac{\\text{adj}(A)}{|A|}$), and Applications of Determinants to solve systems of linear equations (NCERT Section 4.6). (Allocated 2 MCQs + 1 SA (3m) + **1 Long Answer (5m)** = **10 Marks** in the blueprint).\n\nBecause solving linear equations using the adjoint and determinant method uses matrix notation ($AX = B$), it is sometimes colloquially referred to as the \"matrix method\", but in the NCERT syllabus and D.A.V. Blueprint, **it is the standard 5-mark question of Chapter 4 (Determinants)**.\n\n---\n\n### What Has Been Updated in Q32 (Set A & Set B)\n\nTo avoid any ambiguity and make its classification under **Chapter 4: Determinants** unmistakable:\n\n1. **Question Phrasing in Question Papers:**\n   > **Q32.** For the system of linear equations:\n   > $$x + y + z = 6$$\n   > $$y + 3z = 11$$\n   > $$x - 2y + z = 0$$\n   > write the coefficient matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$. **Evaluate the determinant $|A|$, find $\\text{adj}(A)$, determine $A^{-1} = \\frac{\\text{adj}(A)}{|A|}$, and hence solve the system of equations.**\n\n2. **Step-by-Step Mark Breakdown in Marking Schemes:**\n   - **Step 1 (1 Mark):** Evaluating the $3 \\times 3$ **Determinant** $|A| = 9 \\neq 0$.\n   - **Step 2 (1.5 Marks):** Computing all 9 cofactors and the **Adjoint Matrix** $\\text{adj}(A)$.\n   - **Step 3 (0.5 Mark):** Computing the **Inverse Matrix** $A^{-1} = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\text{adj}(A)$.\n   - **Step 4 (2 Marks):** Solving $X = A^{-1}B$ to find $x = 1, y = 2, z = 3$ (Set A) / $x = 2, y = 1, z = 3$ (Set B).\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Section D (4 × 5 Marks = 20 Marks)\n\n| Q. No. | Subject / Chapter | Topic Covered | Marks |\n|:---:|---|---|:---:|\n| **Q32** | **Determinants (Ch 4)** | Evaluation of Determinant $\\|A\\|$, Cofactors, $\\text{adj}(A)$, $A^{-1}$, and System Solution | **5 Marks** |\n| **Q33** | **Continuity & Differentiability (Ch 5)** | Second-order derivative proof: $(1-x^2)y_2 - xy_1 - 2 = 0$ | **5 Marks** |\n| **Q34** | **Application of Derivatives (Ch 6)** | Maxima/Minima optimization: Open box of maximum volume from tin sheet | **5 Marks** |\n| **Q35** | **Integrations (Ch 7)** | Rational integral evaluation using partial fractions $\\int \\frac{P(x)}{Q(x)} dx$ | **5 Marks** |\n\n---\n\n### Access the Updated Files\n\nDirectory: `C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\`\n\n* **Set A Question Paper:** [Set_A_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.docx) | [Text File](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Question_Paper.txt)\n* **Set A Marking Scheme:** [Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.docx) | [Text File](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_A_Marking_Scheme.txt)\n* **Set B Question Paper:** [Set_B_Question_Paper.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.docx) | [Text File](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Question_Paper.txt)\n* **Set B Marking Scheme:** [Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.docx) | [Text File](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/math_exam_2026/Set_B_Marking_Scheme.txt)"}
