{"step_index":167,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T16:34:37Z","thinking":"**Verifying Question Accuracy**\n\nI'm now diving deep into the audit. My focus has sharpened to a question-by-question review of all 38 questions across both Set A and Set B. I'm rigorously verifying the question statements, the embedded numbers, all calculations, and, crucially, confirming the correctness of each answer option. It's meticulous, but vital.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Python script to rigorously verify every numerical calculation, matrix inverse, determinant, derivative, integral, and step marking across Set A and Set B.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nMathematical verification script for Set A and Set B questions and solutions.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport sympy as sp\n\nprint(\"=== AUDITING SET A ===\")\n\n# Q1: R on {1,2,3} = {(1,1),(2,2),(3,3),(1,2)}\n# Reflexive? Yes (1,1),(2,2),(3,3). Symmetric? (1,2) in R but (2,1) not. Transitive? Yes. -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q2: f(x) = x^2 on R. Neither 1-1 nor onto -> (d) Correct.\n\n# Q3: sin^-1(-1/2) = -pi/6 -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q4: domain cos^-1(2x - 1) -> -1 <= 2x-1 <= 1 -> 0 <= 2x <= 2 -> [0, 1] -> (a) Correct.\n\n# Q5: range tan^-1 x is (-pi/2, pi/2) -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q6: A skew-symmetric => a_23 = -a_32 => x = -(-3) = 3 -> (a) Correct.\n\n# Q7: A + A^T is always symmetric -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q8: (AB - BA)^T = B^T A^T - A^T B^T = BA - AB = -(AB - BA) => skew-symmetric -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q9: |3A| = 3^3 |A| = 27 * 5 = 135 -> (c) Correct.\n\n# Q10: |adj A| = |A|^(3-1) = 4^2 = 16 -> (c) Correct.\n\n# Q11: d/dx(e^2x) = 2e^2x -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q12: dA/dr = 2*pi*r at r=5 is 10*pi -> (b) Correct.\n\n# Q13: integral sec^2 x dx = tan x + C -> (a) Correct.\n\n# Q14: integral 1/(1+x^2) dx = tan^-1 x + C -> (a) Correct.\n\n# Q15: integral 1/sqrt(1-x^2) dx = sin^-1 x + C -> (a) Correct.